    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can offer personalized tutoring, explain concepts in everyday language, and adapt to a student’s pace. They can simulate classroom discussions, offer step-by-step problem-solving, and reduce anxiety by making math feel less intimidating. But they must be guided by teachers—humans still provide context, emotional support, and critical thinking."
